      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ARIONROCK (5) gets the nod in a race where the main hopes all bring different queries. He was beaten four and a half metres when fourth as favourite at Bunbury in similar grade, and that first-up run should have him ready to peak in a field lacking a standout last-start profile. MY ULTIMATE KEVVIE (1) is the obvious danger after beating Goodonya Mate by just over six metres at Narrogin, though he now rises from NR up to 50 to NR up to 75. The ace draw and strong local record give him a genuine chance to carry the form across. THE SWINDLER (4) resumes from a six-month break and must improve on two plain winter runs, but a Narrogin track-and-trip win and the better draw keep her in the mix if forward enough. MAJIC BAY (6) has been safely held at his past two, yet the drop from NR 71 to 80 and a solid record at this track and distance make him the most appealing value runner among the main hopes.",
